Q: razor model binding for one to many to many A: <p><strong>Update</strong></p>
<p>Based on your description, from my comprehension, your model would be a <strong>one-to-many</strong> relationship with <strong>one-form-to-many-types</strong>. You'd better consider and express more clearly if the some batch of types could be related to different forms, then it would be many-to-many.</p>
<p>If one-to-many, the relationship is easy to set. EF Core provides a simple way to configure it.</p>
<p>I mocked some models and data. Let's assume the changetypes are some worker information indicating their status.</p>
<p><code>Model.cs</code>:</p>
<pre><code>public class ChangeType
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string? ChangeTypeName { get; set; }
    public bool IsSelected { get; set; } = false;
    public int ChangeFormId { get; set; }
    public ChangeForm? ChangeForm { get; set; }
}

public class ChangeForm
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string? FormName { get; set; }
    public ICollection&lt;ChangeType&gt; ChangeTypes { get; } = new List&lt;ChangeType&gt;();
}
</code></pre>
<p><code>DbContext.cs</code>:</p>
<pre><code>protected override void OnModelCreating(ModelBuilder modelBuilder)
{
    modelBuilder.Entity&lt;ChangeForm&gt;()
        .HasMany(e =&gt; e.ChangeTypes)
        .WithOne(e =&gt; e.ChangeForm)
        .HasForeignKey(e =&gt; e.ChangeFormId)
        .IsRequired();
}

public DbSet&lt;WebApplication81.Models.ChangeType&gt; ChangeType { get; set; } = default!;
public DbSet&lt;WebApplication81.Models.ChangeForm&gt; ChangeForm { get; set; } = default!;
</code></pre>
<p>Index view of <code>ChangeForm</code>:</p>
<pre><code>@model IEnumerable&lt;WebApplication81.Models.ChangeForm&gt;

@{
    ViewData[&quot;Title&quot;] = &quot;Index&quot;;
}

&lt;h1&gt;Index&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;a asp-action=&quot;Create&quot;&gt;Create New&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;table&quot;&gt;
    &lt;thead&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;th&gt;
                @Html.DisplayNameFor(model =&gt; model.FormName)
            &lt;/th&gt;
            &lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
    &lt;/thead&gt;
    &lt;tbody&gt;
        @foreach (var item in Model) {
            &lt;tr&gt;
                &lt;td&gt;
                    @Html.DisplayFor(modelItem =&gt; item.FormName)
                &lt;/td&gt;
                &lt;td&gt;
                    &lt;a asp-action=&quot;Edit&quot; asp-route-id=&quot;@item.Id&quot;&gt;Edit&lt;/a&gt; |
                    &lt;a asp-action=&quot;Details&quot; asp-route-id=&quot;@item.Id&quot;&gt;Details&lt;/a&gt; |
                    &lt;a asp-action=&quot;Delete&quot; asp-route-id=&quot;@item.Id&quot;&gt;Delete&lt;/a&gt;
                &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;/tr&gt;

            &lt;tr&gt;
                &lt;td&gt;
                    @foreach (var type in item.ChangeTypes)
                    {
                        &lt;text&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/text&gt;
                        @Html.HiddenFor(model =&gt; type.Id)
                        @Html.DisplayFor(model =&gt; type.ChangeTypeName)
                        @Html.DisplayFor(model =&gt; type.IsSelected)
                        &lt;a asp-controller=&quot;ChangeTypes&quot; asp-action=&quot;Edit&quot; asp-route-id=&quot;@type.Id&quot;&gt;Edit&lt;/a&gt;
                        &lt;a asp-controller=&quot;ChangeTypes&quot; asp-action=&quot;Details&quot; asp-route-id=&quot;@type.Id&quot;&gt;Details&lt;/a&gt;
                        &lt;a asp-controller=&quot;ChangeTypes&quot; asp-action=&quot;Delete&quot; asp-route-id=&quot;@type.Id&quot;&gt;Delete&lt;/a&gt;
                        &lt;br /&gt;
                    }
                &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;/tr&gt;
        }
    &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>You can see the page of forms and types, whether 1 form or a list is ok. Only some logic in controller is needed for custom design.</p>
